-# DeltaESC G30D v0.6.5 - G30 framing + stock-compatible IAP ACK
+# DeltaESC G30D v0.6.6 - stock dashboard runtime + staged IAP
 
-**UNVALIDATED ON REAL DELTAESC HARDWARE. DO NOT FLASH UNTIL THE READ-ONLY LINK PROBE IS VERIFIED AND THE FIRST-FLASH CHECKLIST IS explicitly approved.**
+Status: **CI/development candidate. Do not flash until the v0.1.0 BLE app compatibility check and first-controller SHU procedure are explicitly approved.**
 
-This supersedes v0.6.4 before first hardware flash.
+Based on the CI-green v0.6.5 staged-IAP/128-byte/VTOR candidate.
 
-Changes vs v0.6.2:
-- G30/Ninebot `5A A5 LEN SRC DST CMD ARG PAYLOAD CK` parser on PA2 USART2.
-- Keeps `55 AA` parser only as a conservative compatibility fallback.
-- Replies in the same framing family received.
-- D0 read has an explicit `DESC` magic signature, protocol 0.2 and build `0x0605`.
-- Read response command on 5A A5 is stock-style `0x04`.
-- Stock-compatible staged IAP `07/08/09/0A` retained; no application-vector invalidation.
-- SAFE build still compiles out bridge arming and motor run.
+## v0.6.6 delta
 
-First hardware goal is deliberately read-only: Android v0.2 pairs through stock dashboard using NinebotCrypto, proves ESC read route, then differentiates stock D0 from DeltaESC D0 by the `DESC` signature. Motor commands are not part of that test.
+- Keeps the v0.6.5 staged IAP implementation, 128-byte data blocks, encrypted-only SHU packaging and explicit VTOR relocation.
+- Adds the native G30 dashboard runtime on PA2 without changing the Android/NinebotCrypto transport.
+- Native `5A A5` dashboard `0x65` frames from `0x21 -> 0x20` are decoded read-only. Throttle is payload byte 1, brake payload byte 2, matching the established G30 VESC/SmartESC integrations.
+- Native dashboard `0x64` requests receive a stock-shaped `0x64` ESC status frame with six bytes: mode, battery, light, beep, speed, fault.
+- The first-test SYNC-SAFE payload deliberately reports Drive, 50% placeholder battery, light off, beep off, speed 0, fault 0. The 50% value is a bench placeholder because bus-voltage calibration remains deferred.
+- Dashboard throttle/brake values are diagnostic only in this step. They do not request torque.
+- D0-D9 diagnostics and E0-E6/F0-F5 protocol remain present; build identity is `0x0606`.
+- App-originated reads no longer falsely count as dashboard-runtime traffic; the dashboard-seen flag now requires native source `0x21`.
 
+## Safety boundary
 
-## v0.6.5 safety delta
-- IAP ACK now matches the user's exact stock DRV126 disassembly: `5A A5 00 20 <dst> 0B <result> CK0 CK1`.
-- ACK `LEN` is 0, command is always `0x0B`, and result is carried in INDEX/ARG.
-- This fixes the v0.6.3 ACK framing blocker; v0.6.3 remains NOT APPROVED for flashing.
-
-
-v0.6.5 hardens the stock IAP transport for 128-byte BLE/PC write frames, accepts only zero padding beyond the advertised final length, tests 8-bit block-index wrap, explicitly relocates VTOR to 0x08001000, and quarantines IAP bytes from the normal app-frame parser while an update is active.
